        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dc7b082f-458b-5dfb-b667-3009232a0cb1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Hightower, Battle of Etowah, Cherokee–American wars, Chickamauga Wars\n- People: Cherokee, Americans, white settlers\n- Places: Old Southwest\n- Topics: frontier conflict, territorial defense, illegal immigration\n\nFacts:\n- The Cherokee–American wars, also called the Chickamauga Wars, were a series of raids, campaigns, ambushes, minor skirmishes, and full-scale frontier battles fought between the Cherokee and Americans from 1776 to 1795 in the Old Southwest.\n- In the Cherokee–American wars, the Cherokee were also identified as Ani-Yunwiya, Nana Waiya, and Tsalagi.\n- In 1793, the Battle of Hightower, also called the Battle of Etowah, was part of the Cherokee–American wars.\n- In 1793, the Cherokee fought in the Battle of Hightower to defend their territory from illegal immigration by white settlers.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
